The Control Center Interface
The Apple iPhone Control Center interface occupies substantially the entire display. The interface consists of a status area at the top of the display, multiple grouped system controls and indicators arranged in a grid, and a vertical column of interface icons positioned along the right edge of the display.
Status Area
At the top of the display, from left to right, the following elements are visible:
•	A plus ("+") symbol positioned in the upper-left corner.
•	The Dynamic Island is centered at the top of the display. A solid red circular indicator is visible toward its left side, consistent with the iOS screen-recording status indicator.
•	A power symbol positioned in the upper-right corner.
Immediately below the status area are:
•	An Airplane Mode status indicator positioned on the left.
•	A battery indicator positioned on the right displaying a battery level of 87%.

The Connectivity Module
The upper-left Control Center module contains a group of connectivity-related controls arranged within a rounded rectangular panel.
The following controls are displayed:
•	Airplane Mode, displayed as an orange circular button with a white airplane symbol, visually indicating an active or enabled state.
•	AirDrop, displayed as a gray circular button with a white AirDrop symbol, indicating an inactive state.
•	Wi-Fi, displayed as a gray circular button containing a Wi-Fi symbol with a diagonal slash through the symbol, indicating an inactive state.
•	Four additional gray circular controls displaying symbols visually consistent with:
•	Cellular communications.
•	Bluetooth.
•	Hot spot, indicating a disabled state.
•	Internet connectivity (globe symbol), indicating an inactive state.

The Media Playback Module
The upper-right Control Center module contains the media playback controls.
The module displays:
•	An empty media artwork placeholder positioned on the left side.
•	An AirPlay output icon positioned in the upper-right corner, indicating an inactive state.
•	The text "Not Playing" displayed beneath the artwork placeholder.
•	A row of media playback controls consisting of:
o	Previous.
o	Play.
o	Next.
The module displays no media title, artist information, or artwork.

The Rotation Lock and Silent Mode Controls
Immediately below the Connectivity Module are two circular system controls.
These controls display symbols visually consistent with:
•	Rotation Lock.
•	Silent Mode.
Each control is displayed as a gray circular button.

The Focus Module
Positioned below the Rotation Lock and Silent Mode controls is a rounded rectangular module labeled "Focus."
The module contains multiple small circular icons representing available Focus modes together with a downward-pointing disclosure indicator.

The Brightness and Volume Controls

Immediately below the Media Playback Module are two vertical slider controls.
The left slider controls screen brightness and displays a sun symbol near its lower end.
The right slider controls system volume and displays a speaker symbol near its lower end.

The Utility Controls
The lower portion of the Control Center contains eight circular system controls arranged in two rows of four controls each.
The controls display symbols visually consistent with:
•	Flashlight.
•	Timer.
•	Calculator.
•	Camera.
•	Screen Mirroring.
•	Code Scanner (QR Scanner).
•	Screen Recording.
•	Notes / Quick Note.
The Screen Recording control displays a red circular recording indicator within the control.

The Right-Edge Interface Icons
Along the right edge of the display is a vertical column of three interface icons.
From top to bottom, the icons consist of:
•	A heart symbol (jump to the main/first page of the interface, the current one).
•	A musical note symbol (jump to the media player).
•	A wireless transmission symbol (jump to the connectivity related controls panel).
